<!-- ========================================== -->
<!-- 3. DATA FLOW DIAGRAMS (DFD)                -->
<!-- ========================================== -->
<h2>3. Data Flow Diagrams (DFD)</h2>

<p>
    A <strong>Data Flow Diagram (DFD)</strong> is a graphical representation of the "flow" of data through an information system. It models the processes, data stores, external entities, and data paths within the <strong>CampusSync ERP</strong> system.
</p>

<h3>3.1 DFD Standard Symbols &amp; Notations</h3>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Symbol Component</th>
            <th>Shape / Notation</th>
            <th>Description &amp; Purpose</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>External Entity</strong></td>
            <td>Rectangle <code>[ Entity Name ]</code></td>
            <td>Sources and destinations of data outside the system boundary (Student, Faculty, Admin, Alumni).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Process</strong></td>
            <td>Circle / Rounded Box <code>( Process Name )</code></td>
            <td>Transformation of data inputs into data outputs (e.g. Generate QR, Grade Marks).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Data Store</strong></td>
            <td>Open-ended Box <code>== [D#] Store Name ==</code></td>
            <td>Data repositories and database tables at rest (e.g. D4 Attendance Records).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Data Flow</strong></td>
            <td>Directed Arrow <code>─── Flow Name ───&gt;</code></td>
            <td>Path along which data moves between entities, processes, and stores.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<hr style="border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1; margin: 25px 0;">

<!-- Level 0 DFD -->
<h3>3.2 Level 0 DFD: Context Analysis Diagram</h3>
<p>
    The <strong>Context Diagram (Level 0 DFD)</strong> establishes the system boundary of CampusSync by demonstrating how external user roles interact directly with the central system engine.
</p>

<div class="diagram-box">
                    ┌─────────────────────────┐
                    │      STUDENT USER       │
                    └───────────┬─────────────┘
                                │ ▲
              1. Login & Scan QR│ │ 2. Live Attendance %,
             3. View Sem Marks  │ │    Notices, Marksheets
                                ▼ │
    ┌───────────────────────────┴─┴───────────────────────────┐
    │                                                         │
    │               0.0 CAMPUSSYNC ERP SYSTEM                 │
    │                 (Core Central Engine)                   │
    │                                                         │
    └───────────┬─▲─────────────────────────────┬─▲───────────┘
                │ │                             │ │
  4. Dynamic QR │ │ 5. Class Registers,         │ │ 8. Verify OTP,
  6. Submit Mark│ │    Subject Lists            │ │    Download PDF
                │ │                             │ │
                ▼ │                             ▼ │
  ┌─────────────┴─┴─────────┐         ┌─────────┴─┴───────────┐
  │      FACULTY USER       │         │  ALUMNI / PUBLIC USER │
  └─────────────────────────┘         └───────────────────────┘
                ▲
                │ 9. Configs, CMS, Master Records
                │ 10. Audit Logs & System Analytics
                ▼
  ┌─────────────────────────┐
  │   ADMINISTRATOR USER    │
  └─────────────────────────┘
</div>

<p><strong>Entity Inflow / Outflow Summary Table:</strong></p>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>External Entity</th>
            <th>Data Inputs (To System)</th>
            <th>Data Outputs (From System)</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Student</strong></td>
            <td>Login credentials, QR code scan data, Profile changes, Password OTP</td>
            <td>Subject-wise attendance percentages, Internal marks, Campus circulars</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Faculty</strong></td>
            <td>Dynamic QR generation requests, Manual attendance, Internal marks</td>
            <td>Assigned student lists, Official registers, Course syllabus details</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Administrator</strong></td>
            <td>Master student/faculty accounts, Course setup, Notices, Gallery images, CMS</td>
            <td>Institution pass-rate analytics, Audit logs, System status</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Alumni / Public</strong></td>
            <td>Enrollment number, Semester, Email OTP verification, General inquiries</td>
            <td>Consolidated semester marksheet PDF, Public photo gallery, Announcements</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<!-- Level 1 DFD -->
<h3>3.3 Level 1 DFD: Decomposed Functional Modules</h3>
<p>
    Level 1 DFD breaks down <strong>0.0 CampusSync ERP</strong> into its 6 primary sub-processes and maps them to respective database tables.
</p>

<div class="diagram-box">
  [ STUDENT ] ──(Credentials)──&gt; ( 1.0 Authentication ) &lt;──[ D1 Students ]
  [ FACULTY ] ──(Credentials)──&gt; (     &amp; Security     ) &lt;──[ D2 Faculty ]
  [ ADMIN   ] ──(Credentials)──&gt; (    Management      ) &lt;──[ D3 Admins ]
                                           │
                        Session Auth Token │
                                           ▼
  [ FACULTY ] ──(Lecture Info)─&gt; ( 2.0 Smart QR &amp;      ) ──(Log Attendance)──&gt; [ D4 AttendanceRecords ]
  [ STUDENT ] ──(Scan QR Data)─&gt; ( Attendance Engine   ) ──(Update %)────────&gt; [ D1 Students ]
                                           │
  [ FACULTY ] ──(Unit Test/Assn)&gt;( 3.0 Internal Marks  ) ──(Save Scores)─────&gt; [ D5 InternalMarks ]
  [ STUDENT ] &lt;─(View Results)── ( &amp; Academic Grading  ) ──(Syllabus Credits)&gt; [ D6 Subjects ]
                                           │
  [ ADMIN   ] ──(New Notice)───&gt; ( 4.0 Circulars &amp;     ) ──(Store Post)──────&gt; [ D7 Notifications ]
  [ PUBLIC  ] &lt;─(Read Notice)─── ( Notice Board System )
                                           │
  [ ADMIN   ] ──(Upload Photo)─&gt; ( 5.0 Campus Gallery  ) ──(Save Images)─────&gt; [ D8 GalleryItems ]
  [ ADMIN   ] ──(Banner/CMS)───&gt; ( &amp; Homepage CMS      ) ──(Save Settings)───&gt; [ D9 HomePageSettings ]
                                           │
  [ ALUMNI  ] ──(Enrollment/OTP)&gt;( 6.0 Alumni Result   ) ──(Fetch History)───&gt; [ D10 ArchivedStudents ]
  [ ALUMNI  ] &lt;─(Download PDF)── ( Verification Engine ) ──(Generate PDF)────&gt; [ D11 ArchivedMarks ]
</div>

<p><strong>Core Processes in Level 1 DFD:</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>1.0 Authentication &amp; Security:</strong> Validates user role (Student, Faculty, Admin), verifies hashed passwords, manages session timeouts.</li>
    <li><strong>2.0 Smart QR &amp; Attendance Engine:</strong> Dynamic QR generation with countdown timers to eliminate proxy attendance.</li>
    <li><strong>3.0 Internal Marks &amp; Grading:</strong> Calculates continuous evaluation (Unit tests, assignments, attendance component).</li>
    <li><strong>4.0 Circulars &amp; Notice Board:</strong> Disseminates institutional notices filtered by target audience.</li>
    <li><strong>5.0 Campus Gallery &amp; Homepage CMS:</strong> Full-resolution photo gallery with categorization and live home page content editor.</li>
    <li><strong>6.0 Alumni Result Verification:</strong> Secure historical marksheet retrieval using Two-Factor Email OTP verification.</li>
</ul>

<hr style="border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1; margin: 25px 0;">

<!-- Level 2 DFD -->
<h3>3.4 Level 2 DFD: Smart QR-based Attendance Flow (Process 2.0)</h3>
<p>
    This diagram details the real-time operational flow of the QR-based smart attendance subsystem (Process 2.0).
</p>

<div class="diagram-box">
  [ Faculty User ]
         │
         ▼ (Select Subject &amp; Division)
  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ 2.1 Generate Dynamic QR Session                        │
  │     - Assign unique session UUID                       │
  │     - Set expiry window (e.g. 15-30 seconds)           │
  │     - Display live QR code on classroom projector      │
  └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                             │ (Session Token)
                             ▼
  [ Student Mobile Device ]  │
         │                   │
         ▼ (Scan Live QR via Camera)
  ┌──────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┐
  │ 2.2 Validate QR Scan Request                           │
  │     - Check Session Expiry (Timestamp &lt; ExpireTime)    │
  │     - Check Student Enrollment &amp; Division Match        │
  │     - Check Duplicate Scan (Anti-Proxy Engine)         │
  └──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┘
                             │
            ┌────────────────┴────────────────┐
            ▼ [Valid Scan]                    ▼ [Invalid / Expired]
  ┌───────────────────────────────┐  ┌───────────────────────────────┐
  │ 2.3 Record Presence           │  │ 2.4 Reject Scan               │
  │     - Insert into D4 Database │  │     - Alert Student Device    │
  │     - Method: 'QR'            │  │     - Log Security Warning    │
  │     - Status: 'Present'       │  └───────────────────────────────┘
  └──────────────┬────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
  ┌───────────────────────────────┐
  │ 2.5 Recalculate %             │
  │     - Present Lectures / Total│
  │     - Push update to Student  │
  └───────────────────────────────┘
</div>

<p><strong>Sub-process Logic Highlights:</strong></p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Dynamic Expiration:</strong> QR codes rotate on faculty screens to prevent unauthorized sharing outside classroom.</li>
    <li><strong>Anti-Proxy Constraint:</strong> A student cannot scan twice for the same lecture session.</li>
    <li><strong>Dual Mode Fallback:</strong> If a student has camera/device failure, faculty can mark attendance via the Manual Register view.</li>
</ol>

<br>
